From 0f1f2662d8c0c47ccc8dcadfe3821399652c4aa4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Damien Dusha <Damien Dusha>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 22:31:08 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] stats: print the [LOG-LCKD] prefix only when the line behind
 it prints

The prefix was missing the state-change term that gates the message it
prefixes:

    CLILOG(S.logging.logid && S.logging.locked, "[LOG-LCKD] ");
    CLILOG(S.logging.locked && (locked != S.stats.locked), "PTP %s!\n", ...);

ptp_collect_stats() runs once per Sync, so the prefix printed every cycle and
the message almost never did.

Measured on a NUCLEO-H563ZI with `ptp log logid on` and `ptp log locked on`
and every other logging flag off, 25 seconds of console:

  before:  [LOG-LCKD] [LOG-LCKD] [LOG-LCKD] [LOG-LCKD] ... 25 of them, nothing else
  after:   (silent)

and across a cold acquisition, where the lock state genuinely does change:

  [LOG-LCKD] PTP LOCKED!
  [LOG-LCKD] PTP DIVERGED!

with no orphan prefixes -- so the prefix still marks every real transition and
only those.

The condition is lifted into a named local rather than repeated, so the two
CLILOGs cannot drift apart again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/flexptp/stats.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/flexptp/stats.c b/src/flexptp/stats.c
index dab7be6..bd512d7 100644
--- a/src/flexptp/stats.c
+++ b/src/flexptp/stats.c
@@ -39,8 +39,12 @@ void ptp_collect_stats(int64_t d) {
 
 	// set locked state
 	bool locked = ((fabs(S.stats.filtTimeErr) < (PTP_ACCURACY_LIMIT_NS)) && (ptp_get_current_master_clock_identity() != 0));
-	CLILOG(S.logging.logid && S.logging.locked, "[LOG-LCKD] ");
-	CLILOG(S.logging.locked && (locked != S.stats.locked), "PTP %s!\n", locked ? "LOCKED" : "DIVERGED");
+	// The prefix carries the SAME condition as the line it prefixes. Without the state-change
+	// term it printed on every call -- and ptp_collect_stats() runs once per Sync -- so the
+	// console filled with bare "[LOG-LCKD] " markers and no messages behind them.
+	bool lockStateChanged = (locked != S.stats.locked);
+	CLILOG(S.logging.logid && S.logging.locked && lockStateChanged, "[LOG-LCKD] ");
+	CLILOG(S.logging.locked && lockStateChanged, "PTP %s!\n", locked ? "LOCKED" : "DIVERGED");
 	
 	// invoke LOCKED/UNLOCKED event
 	if (locked != S.stats.locked) {
